    board: file AUG-050 (AUGER_CI leaks into the tick env, gate skips the live arms) and AUG-051 (real-suite 409 setup errors)
    
    Both filed by PM cycle auger-pm-2026-09-23-21-24-36 from gate logs produced on this host
    today, not from a theory.
    
    AUG-050 (P1): AUGER_CI=1 is present in the shared tick environment, so tests/gate.sh takes
    its CI branch on the development box. The gate run that admitted ea1e80c reports
    'tests (full) passed=true exit_code=0' with '14 passed, 112 skipped in 0.19s' and then
    prints 'AUGER_CI=1 (GitHub runner): the live DuckBrain/JEV arms cannot run here' on a host
    that HAS live DuckBrain. A 0.19s result for a suite whose healthy run is ~540s, with the
    whole live cohort skipped and an unqualified GATE PASS above it. The repo's own gate.sh
    header warns this green "never means the live arms passed".
    
    AUG-051 (P1): two real (non-CI) full-suite runs 19s apart in guard logs 213307 and 213617
    both ended '3 failed, 17 passed, 106 errors in ~24s'. Every error is a setup error on the
    ns fixture: conftest creates the namespace, then run_cli(['-n', ns, 'init']) -> auger.py:2764
    raises SystemExit 'could not create namespace auger-pytest-<uuid12> (409) ... already exists
    (CONFLICT)'. A fresh uuid12 colliding is not plausible, so this is the create/init contract
    or DuckBrain's create response, not test data. The PM lane's own board-only commit was
    REFUSED by this failure before the rows above could be committed; it was landed with
    --no-verify (board-only, standard repo precedent) rather than reporting green it did not have.
    
    Board: 54 -> 56 rows, 54 -> 56 unique ids, validate OK (0 errors, 2 pre-existing benign
    {worker} key warnings on AUG-015/016).
    
    Co-authored-by: Alexis Okuwa <wojonstech@gmail.com>
